   214	 * comments and strings.  Loops that handle an entire token within
   215	 * their scope also gather entire strings and pass them to
   216	 * printbuf_memappend() in a single call, rather than calling
   217	 * printbuf_memappend() one char at a time.
   218	 *
   219	 * PEEK_CHAR() and ADVANCE_CHAR() macros are used for code that is
   220	 * common to both the main loop and the tighter loops.
