ogate and the incomplete low surrogate, and not add any replacement char.\n\nBut the code adds a replacement char anyway. This is the "unnecessarily added" behavior.\n\nOK, I think I understand the vulnerability now. Let me create a PoC that triggers this behavior and submit it.\n\nThe PoC should be a JSON input that:\n1. Contains a string with a high surrogate unicode escape (`\\uD834`)\n2. Followed by `\\u` (indicating the start of the low surrogate)\n3. But then the input ends (or the low surrogate is incomplete)\n\nThis will trigger the code path where:\n- got_hi_surrogate is set\n- We find the next `\\u`\n- We skip `\\u`\n- Input runs out before we complete the low surrogate\n- We add a replacement char unnecessarily\n\nLet me create this PoC and test it.', action=<ActionType.THINK: 'think'>)
